# Extra specs for the `cuda13` flavor (one per line; `#` comments allowed).
# Added via `spack add` on top of the base environment. cuda_arch=75 comes from
# flavors/cuda13.yaml.

# CUDA toolkit, provided by Spack (no vendor base image needed). The build only
# needs nvcc/headers; no physical GPU is required to compile.
#
# The version has a floor set by the image this flavor runs on, and picking it
# too low fails at concretization ("Cannot find a valid provider for virtual c"
# for the entire stack, because nothing can provide the host compiler):
#   * gcc 15 (ubuntu26.04) needs cuda@13:  -- `%gcc@15: conflicts %cuda@:12.9`
#   * glibc 2.42+ (ubuntu26.04 has 2.43) needs cuda@13.1: -- the C23 exception
#     specifications of cospi/sinpi/rsqrt changed in glibc 2.41
# Re-check both when moving this flavor to a different base image or compiler.
cuda@13.3.0

# cuDNN, needed by ONNX Runtime's CUDA execution provider, which links it but
# does not bundle it. The `-13` suffix is the CUDA 13 build: the package maps it
# to `depends_on("cuda@13")`, so it unifies with the toolkit above rather than
# dragging in a second CUDA. Keep the two in step when bumping either.
cudnn@9.21.0.82-13

# TensorRT, for ACTS' Gnn plugin (it deserializes prebuilt .engine files). Not
# in upstream Spack; spack_repo/acts/packages/tensorrt unpacks NVIDIA's debs.
# It lives in this flavor rather than one of its own: a split would duplicate
# the far larger cuda + cudnn download (~4.9 GB) across two stacks to avoid
# carrying TensorRT in one.
#
# Most of TensorRT is builder weight that ACTS never uses — it only calls
# createInferRuntime and deserializeCudaEngine. `builder=` keeps just the
# per-architecture builder resource for this flavor's own target, taking the
# install from 2628 MB to 922 MB while leaving every library and symbol ACTS
# links exactly as shipped. Keep it in step with cuda_arch in cuda13.yaml:
# sm75 here is the same Turing target. `builder=none` would save a further
# 111 MB but then no engine can be built at all, which is a bet on nothing in
# the stack ever calling the builder — hence the conservative choice.
#
# The download is ~1.9 GB either way: NVIDIA ships every builder resource
# inside the one libnvinfer11 deb, so trimming only shrinks the installed tree,
# the buildcache entry and the image — the costs that recur.
#
# `runtime=lean` would be 106 MB, but it is not reachable from where ACTS is:
# it has no plugin library, and ACTS calls initLibNvInferPlugins and links
# trt::nvinfer_plugin, whose DT_NEEDED on libnvinfer pulls the full library
# back regardless. It would also need FindTensorRT to resolve nvinfer_lean and
# engines built version compatible. Flip it here if those ever land upstream.
tensorrt@11.1.0.106 runtime=full builder=sm75

# traccc GPU tracking R&D stack. ACTS vendors traccc and detray in its own tree
# (Traccc/, Detray/, pulled in with add_subdirectory) and FetchContents
# algebra-plugins under thirdparty/, so none of the three belongs here: there is
# no ACTS_USE_SYSTEM_DETRAY, algebra-plugins has no system option at all, and
# Spack carries no traccc package in the first place. What ACTS does take from
# the environment is vecmem and covfie, at versions it pins exactly
# (_acts_vecmem_version 1.25.0, _acts_covfie_version 0.15.2). Spack's newest
# vecmem is 1.25.0, so that one has no headroom — re-check both when ACTS moves.
vecmem@1.25.0+cuda
covfie@0.15.6+cuda

# Alpaka, for traccc's portability backend (TRACCC_BUILD_ALPAKA). `backend=cuda`
# rather than `cuda_only`, which conflicts with every other backend and would
# drop the serial one. alpaka is a CudaPackage, so cuda_arch=75 from
# cuda13.yaml applies here too.
alpaka backend=cuda

# Deliberately absent:
#   cccl     CUDA 13.3 already ships CCCL 3.3.3 (lib64/cmake/thrust), and traccc
#            pins 2.7.0 in extern/cccl while warning against nvcc picking up the
#            toolkit copy. Taking it from cuda here; reconciling that pin is a
#            downstream question.
#   vc       ACTS sets ALGEBRA_PLUGINS_INCLUDE_VC FALSE and detray's Vc plugins
#            (DETRAY_VC_{AOS,SOA}_PLUGIN) default OFF, so nothing asks for it.
#            Spack has vc@1.4.5 — detray's exact DETRAY_VC_VERSION — if it
#            ever gets switched on.
#   dfelibs  dead upstream; the parts still in use are to be vendored instead.
